# iOS environments

`createIosTargetsForEnvs` in `ios-targets.js` is one fragile algorithm (~2k lines). **Do not** split or “clean up” its internals unless the user asked to change that algorithm.

Mechanical file moves are OK. Behavior-changing regex/pbxproj edits need a failing test or an explicit request.

Android env flavors live in `android.js` (`copyAndroidEnvSources`, `updateAndroidBuildGradle`) and are already called from `apply.js`.
